<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.3.1: Quadratic Expressions and Area</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01776</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.3.1: Quadratic Expressions and Area</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e445fa45-16c0-475b-aa85-915a774efe82</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Figure A is a large square. Figure B is a large square with a smaller square removed. Figure C is composed of two
  large squares with one smaller square added.</para>
<para>Figure A</para>
<para><figure><media alt="A square."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d28af56f9faeb2db1a12d7156f3528814ed815e4"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Figure B</para>
<para><figure><media alt="A square with a 1 by 1 square removed from the lower left interior."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c3cfac891ace1f56f136f8b22a4de52ec5fbcbce"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Figure C</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Two large squares connected on the right side to a one by one smaller square."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1aee0b31bb1dccc91cbffadcad11bc90255ad88c"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Write an expression to represent the area of each shaded figure when the side length of the large square is as shown
  in the first column.</para>
<para>Copy and complete the table. Compare your work by answering 1 - 12.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        Side length of
        large square
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        Area of A
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        Area of B
      </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        Area of C
      </emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\(4\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\(x\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\(4x\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>\(x+3\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
      <entry/>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>


<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4\), what is the area of figure A? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(4^2\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4\), what is the area of figure B? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(4^2-1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4\), what is the area of figure C? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(2(4^2)+1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x\), what is the area of figure A? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^2\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x\), what is the area of figure B? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^2-1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x\), what is the area of figure C? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(2x^2+1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4x\), what is the area of figure A? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(16x^2\) or \((4x)^2\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4x\), what is the area of figure B? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(16x^2-1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(4x\), what is the area of figure C? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(32x^2+1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x+3\), what is the area of figure A? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\((x+3)^2\) or \((x+3)(x+3)\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x+3\), what is the area of figure B? </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\((x+3)^2-1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> When the side length of the large square is \(x+3\), what is the area of figure C </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(2(x+3)^2+1\) (or an equivalent expression)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
